- batch.gen

This file illustrates how to use mkdata to achieve batch data generation.

New method: Use Generators for concise code.
@run {
    # The Generator.int_progression preset creates an int array that optionally attatches noise at runtime
    % generator: Generator.int_progression([10] * 4 + [1000] * 6, noise_ratio = 0.2)
    # [generator].size is available on instances which sample from a finite iterator
    @for idx in generator.size {
        @redirect f"{idx + 1}.in"
        n: generator.next()  \n    # outputs n
        @loop n {
            rint(1, n)
        }
        \n
    }
}

